   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase Out Management Plan (Stage I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HPMP Phase Out Management Plan in Uganda It is envisaged that the project will enable Uganda to meet the 2013 HCFC freeze, 10% reduction target by 2015, and 35% reduction target by 2020, respectively. Uganda being an Article-5 country under the Montreal Protocol is obligated to phase out the production and consumption of HCFCs through implementing a HCFC Phase-out Management Plan (HPMP) based on a staged approach.  Overall Objective: Attaining both ozone and climate benefits through implementing an Integrated Plan for reducing HCFCs consumption in all sectors and with initial emphasis placed on the refrigeration and air-conditioning sector, as well as promoting and adopting ozone-friendly, climate-friendly, and energy efficient technologies in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
